 is shocked and doesn't believe a word of it. Aya, a friend of Akira, forgets something in the school one night, and asks Akira to help her and go find it. He agrees, and while there, he gets attacked by a shadow monster. Shirogane convinces him that the balance between the human world and the shadow world has been distorted and that Akira must become a \"shin\"- a creature of the shadow world- in order to help restore the balance. The anime has shonen-ai themes which are completely absent from the manga.\n\n(Source: Wikipedia)"},"tags":[{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Slapstick","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Shoujo","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Urban Fantasy","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Age Gap","rank":60,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Boys' Love","rank":44,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Monochrome Factor","english":null,"native":"モノクローム･ファクター","romaji":"Monochrome Factor","synonyms":[{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"幻影少年"}]},"trailer":null,"visibility":"general"}